From 98853033739b1d56654ad40df4674bb491c7ff5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:03:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 44/54] fix-data-6: R-1/R-3 operations and data-center
 families, R-2 lead associates are Mid, K-1 stated bonus targets as posted,
 P-1 pay places named, P-2 exact posted pay on the job page

R-1/R-3 (public/features/roles.js): site-ops, 'Warehouse, delivery & store
operations' (29 families): Amazon's associates, process assistants and lead
associates by title, its area and station managers by department; a data-center
department beats a loose title word (subject matter experts, asset management,
Critical Environment Ops, DCO techs). 1,839 postings change family, none loses
one; Amazon postings with no family 2,332 -> 881.

R-2 (server/keywords.js): 'Lead Associate' and lead before an associate title
is Mid by title, not Senior: 126 postings (Amazon 124, Anduril 2).

K-1: extras.bonusTarget, a stated bonus-target percentage as posted; the chip
reads '+ 20% bonus target', '+ bonus mentioned' only with no figure.

P-1 (public/app.js payPlaceText): pay posted for some of a posting's places
(salary.places) names them under a Location filter, the country only when they
are in another country; the drawer's line fits one line.

P-2: the job page's heading and Pay by place rows give a stated yearly figure
exactly ('$119,800-234,700'), the card's rounded form only where it would wrap.

norm-14 (one bump with G-1); golden re-baselined once from norm-13 (2 of 300).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
